{
  "id": "yi_haicaiqiang",
  "name": "Haicaiqiang (Shiping Yi sea-vegetable tune)",
  "family": "global",
  "lineage": "Song form of the Nisu Yi villages around Yilong Lake in Shiping county, Honghe, also called daobanjiang ('rowing back the oar'), named after the lake's 'sea vegetable' water plant. A complete performance is a large multi-section vocal suite (juqiang, kongqiang, zhengqiqiang and baihuaqiang sections) combining solo, antiphonal, leader-and-chorus, unison and choral singing; tied to a courting custom of young men and women, it was listed in the first batch of China's national intangible-heritage register.",
  "recipe": "classic modern haicaiqiang, ballad Poetry. multi note runs per syllable, many notes per syllable, single leader group response. field recording. ORTF stereo pair, portable field-recorder pre. 24-bit digital.",
